--!strict
--[[
	Config
	Every tunable number in the game lives here. Nothing else should hardcode
	a balance value -- if you find yourself typing a number in a service,
	it probably belongs in this file instead.

	All values are starting points from the design doc and expected to move
	once real players touch the game.
]]

-- A NOTE ON EVERY `tone` IN THIS FILE.
--
-- They are `Theme`'s accent family and they are written out as numbers here
-- rather than required, because Config requires NOTHING -- it is pure data,
-- pulled in by every server service, and making it depend on a UI module to
-- name a colour would be the wrong trade by a distance.
--
-- The family is derived, so a new tone is not a taste decision: take the hue
-- you want and build it at saturation 0.72, value 0.90 -- or value 0.82 if
-- the hue falls between 80 and 200, because green and lime read much
-- brighter than red and blue at the same value. Four tones sit off it on
-- purpose and each says why at its own entry: money is the real GOLD, the
-- prank is pulled back from a pure magenta, hiding is deliberately a neutral,
-- and the shop door and the alien recovery are moved off GOOD's own green so
-- that four different meanings are not one colour.

local Config = {}

-- ============================================================
-- ECONOMY
-- ============================================================

-- Coins added to the vault per second, before upgrades and rebirths.
Config.BASE_INCOME = 10000

-- THE PIG IS UNBOUNDED (designer decision, 2026-09-21, reaffirmed). There
-- is no capacity: `data.coins` has no ceiling, nothing clamps a mint, and the
-- Bigger Piggy Bank tree is retired. Cash resets at every rebirth and rebirth
-- is required for progress, so the RESET bounds hoarding rather than the pig.
-- `BASE_CAPACITY`, the four `CAPACITY_*` growths, `CAPACITY_BASE_COST`,
-- `UPGRADE_COST_CEILING`, `REBIRTH_CAPACITY_MULTIPLE`, `getCapacity`,
-- `getCapacityCost`, `pigRoom` and `fitInPig` are all gone with it. What a
-- pig reads as FULL on the lawn is now the rebirth cash gate -- see
-- `Config.pigFullAt`.

-- Each income upgrade multiplies the rate by this.
Config.INCOME_GROWTH = 1.35

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- TWO BANDS
--
-- THE LADDER IS TWO CURVES, NOT ONE, AND BAND A IS UNTOUCHED ON PURPOSE.
--
-- Levels 1-20 keep exactly the growth they always had: the first two hours of
-- this game were never the problem and that curve is well tuned. Levels 21-40
-- are a second band with GENTLER growth on both sides -- income and cost --
-- because a single curve extended to 40 does not work in either direction.
-- At 1.35 income the rate reaches 121K/s and trivialises everything; at 1.55
-- cost the top level runs to 10.6B and nobody ever buys it.
--
-- The gap between the two growth rates is what sets pacing: cost outruns
-- income by 1.55/1.35 = 14.8% per level in band A, and by 1.26/1.16 = 8.6% in
-- band B. Each level takes longer than the last in both, more gently up top,
-- which is what keeps a 168M purchase feeling like a goal instead of a wall.
Config.BAND_TOP = 20
Config.INCOME_GROWTH_B = 1.16
Config.INCOME_COST_GROWTH_B = 1.26

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- BAND C
--
-- (THE CAPACITY HALF OF THIS BAND IS RETIRED with the pig's ceiling; the
-- paragraph below is kept as the record of why the INCOME half runs to 60,
-- which stands unchanged.)
--
-- THE THIRD BAND EXISTS SO A 1B HOUSE CAN FIT IN A PIG, AND NOTHING BELOW
-- LEVEL 40 MOVED TO MAKE ROOM FOR IT.
--
-- The catalogue was asked to reach 1B and the largest pig this game could
-- produce was 96,904,045. Steepening band B would have got there at level 40
-- -- and measured, it balloons the fill time to 43 minutes, compresses the
-- whole climb into today's 17 days, and rewrites every existing level-21-40
-- save's capacity and income. So the ladder grew instead: levels 41-60, two
-- per rebirth to rebirth 20, and `banded()` below keeps A and B exactly as
-- they were -- every value for level <= 40 and rebirth <= 10 is
-- byte-identical to the day before this landed, which is the whole reason
-- there is no value migration.
--
-- BOTH GROWTH NUMBERS ARE DERIVED, NOT CHOSEN. 1.136 is
-- (1.25e9 / 96,904,045) ^ (1/20): twenty rungs that put the top pig at
-- ~1.24B, so a 1B house sits at 80% of it -- the same headroom the Sky
-- Castle keeps today at 83%. 1.10 is what holds the fill time at the ceiling
-- inside 12-18 minutes against a rebirth multiplier that keeps climbing; the
-- 1.033/level gap between capacity and income growth is what stops the top of
-- the game accelerating. The cost growths are band B's: the affordability
-- clamp binds on every band-C rung (cost/pig reads 0.80 and 0.55 at 40-60),
-- so the curve only has to keep outrunning the pig, and 1.16 > 1.136 does.
--
-- Every number here is regenerable: `docs/LATE-GAME-ECONOMY-PLAN.md` and
-- `tests/sim/late-game/`.
Config.BAND_TOP_2 = 40
Config.INCOME_GROWTH_C = 1.10
Config.INCOME_COST_GROWTH_C = 1.26

-- The hard ceiling. What a player can actually reach is `Config.maxLevel`,
-- which is lower until they have rebirthed enough -- see the note there.
-- 60 puts the top pig at ~1.24B; see BAND C above for the derivation.
Config.ABSOLUTE_MAX_LEVEL = 60

-- Levels a single rebirth adds to the reachable ceiling.
Config.LEVELS_PER_REBIRTH = 2

-- Cost of the first upgrade. Must be reachable in under a minute --
-- the first win has to land immediately.
Config.INCOME_BASE_COST = 400000

-- Cost multiplier per level owned.
Config.INCOME_COST_GROWTH = 1.55

-- ------------------------------------------------- THE AFFORDABILITY CEILING
--
-- RETIRED WITH THE CAPACITY CEILING. `UPGRADE_COST_CEILING` clamped every
-- income and capacity rung to a share of the pig, and its whole reason was
-- the BOUNDED wallet: with a balance capped by capacity a price above your
-- rate was a WALL, because the coins could never be held at one time, and
-- the ladder deadlocked at level 17 of 20 without it (CLAUDE.md, "SO A RUNG
-- IS CLAMPED TO A SHARE OF THE PIG"). With no cap a price above your rate is
-- a WAIT again, which is the ordinary shape of a ladder, so the clamp is
-- gone and `getIncomeCost` is the pure geometric curve at every level. What
-- that costs: the late rungs are dearer than the clamped figures nobody
-- could pay were cheap -- level 20 is 1,653,340 against a clamped 1,643,483
-- and level 40 is 168.2M against 53.3M -- and the "17 days at 2h/day" climb
-- recorded in CLAUDE.md and `tests/sim/late-game/` was measured WITH the
-- clamp and is void rather than re-measured.

-- ============================================================
-- OFFLINE ACCRUAL
-- ============================================================

-- Vault keeps filling while logged off, up to this many seconds.
-- 8 hours deliberately covers a school day, so an after-school player
-- always comes back to a full vault. Income never decays past the cap.
Config.OFFLINE_CAP_SECONDS = 8 * 60 * 60

